{
  "_source": "HCM 7th Edition, Chapter 34 (Interchange Ramp Terminals: Supplemental), Example Problem 3: Diamond Interchange with Queue Spillback (Exhibits 34-30 through 34-43). I-95 at 22nd Avenue, pretimed three-phase diamond, C = 120 s, PHF = 0.97, D = 300 ft, 6.1% heavy vehicles on the external and internal through movements, 2% grade on the NB and SB ramps, turn radii 75 ft (EB/WB internal left) and 50 ft (all other turns). Green intervals reproduce the Exhibit 34-36 movement table with both offsets zero: Intersection I phases 0-27 / 32-91 / 96-115 (NEMA 4+7, 2+6, 1+6) and Intersection II phases 0-27 / 32-71 / 76-115 (NEMA 2+5, 2+6, 3+8). Each internal through movement holds its NEMA phase across two consecutive intersection phases and is therefore entered as one uninterrupted green (EB internal 0-71 s at Intersection II, WB internal 32-115 s at Intersection I). Arrival types reproduce the Exhibit 34-39 progression ratios: Rp = 1.333 (Arrival Type 4) on the two internal through movements, Rp = 1.000 (Arrival Type 3) everywhere else. Extra distance traveled along each freeway ramp is 60 ft at 35 mi/h (EDTT = +/-1.2 s/veh, Exhibit 34-43).",
  "_deviation_ext_right": "The two exclusive external right-turn lane groups (EB EXT-R and WB EXT-R of Exhibits 34-34 / 34-39 / 34-41) have no slot in InterchangeMovement, so this fixture carries the ten lane groups the enum can name and drops the right-turn groups. Setting eb/wb_external_right_shared = false removes O-D F / G from the external through group demand, which is what the published example does (v = 2,062 EB and 1,052 WB exclude the right turns), but it also makes O-D F and O-D G free-flowing rather than signalized. See the gap note in tests/chapter23_integration.rs.",
  "_deviation_lane_utilization": "lane_utilization_override carries the published Exhibit 34-33 values (0.6005 EB / 0.7506 WB). The published %V_Lmax includes the right-turn O-D in the Equation 23-17 approach total (EB: 1/3 - 0.245 x 309/2371 + 0.465 x 1294/2371 = 0.5551) even though the right turn has an exclusive lane, while the engine ties the v_R term of Equation 23-17 to the same eb/wb_external_right_shared flag that governs the lane group demand.",
  "_deviation_eb_internal_left": "demand_override_veh_h = 67 on EbIntLeft reproduces the published lane group analysis, which is not demand-conserving with the published O-D table. Exhibit 34-32 gives O-D E = 1,255 veh/h (1,294 PHF-adjusted) and Exhibits 34-39 / 34-41 analyze the EB internal left at v = 67 veh/h; the internal link then receives 2,062 + 58 veh/h and discharges 826 + 67 veh/h. The Exhibit 34-30 plan view carries two overlapping labels on the EB internal through arrows, 801 and 1991, which are the two mutually exclusive readings of the same movement (801 = I + D with I = 745 and E = 1,255; 1991 = I + D with I = 1,935 and E = 65). Exhibits 34-39 through 34-43 use I = 745 for the O-D demands and 67 veh/h for the internal left, so the fixture does the same.",
